  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "The legacy flat `DocumentNode` / `BlockNode` / `SpanNode` schema was entirely eliminated.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR00Z",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000K",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR010",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Designed and implemented a universal, recursive `BlockNode` topology (Fractal Ontology) rooted in `ArtifactNode`.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR011",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000N",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR012",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Schema updated to pure JSON-LD (`schema.json`), avoiding TypeScript interface duplication.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR013",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000Q",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR014",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "IDs & content fingerprint — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1). `web/src/lib/snowflake.ts` generates the 64-bit Snowflake-style identifier (timestamp + machine identity w/ personal failover + sequence counter, 13-char Crockford Base32); `astParser.ts` uses it for every `blockId` instead of the old content hash. `ArtifactNode.contentHash` renamed to `fileHash` throughout (`artifacts.ts`, `schema.json`) to match §1.B's file-domain-only fingerprint — no structural/recursive hash. Verified live: cleared stale pre-redesign `ArtifactNode`/`BlockNode` docs, ran `kg:track`+`kg:ingest` across all 8 artifacts (1144 blocks total, including a 648-block single-artifact burst), zero id collisions. Also found and fixed a real pre-existing bug while verifying: `getArtifactRecord` treated a missing document's raw 404 response (a string, not a thrown error) as a valid record, so untracked artifacts silently reported \"unchanged\" instead of erroring. Reconciliation (best-effort content matching, §1.C history in Appendix F) remains unimplemented — no code needed it yet, since ingestion so far has only ever run against uningested artifacts.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR015",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000S",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR016",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Ingestion (`astParser.ts` and `artifacts.ts`) now parses Markdown into a deeply nested tree structure and commits the entire fractal tree via `ArtifactNode.root` in a single TerminusDB operation. Note: a plain `getDocument` read only ever returns `root`/`children` as reference ids, not the nested tree, so full-tree reads go through `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (`graphql.ts`) instead — deliberately, not because the Document API is incapable of it (see `Aperas-architecture.md` §2's \"Read-path note\" for the full investigation, including a filed upstream bug, [terminusdb/terminusdb#2512](https://github.com/terminusdb/terminusdb/issues/2512)).",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR017",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000V",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR018",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`FolderNode` — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §4.A). `web/src/lib/folders.ts` walks `AperasKG/artifacts/`, builds one `FolderNode` per directory, absorbs each directory's own `README.md` (parsed blocks become the folder's children; the file itself is never exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`), and references nested `FolderNode`s/`ArtifactNode`s by id. Wired into `npm run kg:ingest`, which now rebuilds the whole folder tree in the same run as artifact ingestion. Added one concrete `Assertion` class (inherits the previously-uninstantiable abstract `BaseEdge`) to `schema.json`, needed to let `crud.ts`/`woql.ts` actually write/query extrinsic edges — documented in `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.D. **As-built today, both `FolderNode` and `ArtifactNode` are still Lexical-keyed on `path`** — the design has since moved to Snowflake ids for both (§4.A/§4.B, Appendix G), but that change isn't implemented yet; tracked under \"Reconciliation matching for re-ingestion\" below, since it's a prerequisite for that work, not this one.",
    "title": "00C5FPAHF000W",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-29T01:19:00.916Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000X",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01A",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`crud.ts`/`woql.ts`/`graphql.ts`/`verifyPhase0.ts` — **migrated off the dead pre-redesign schema and live-verified**. `crud.ts` now provides `insertAssertion`/`deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` for the new `Assertion` type; `woql.ts` queries `Assertion.source`/`predicate`/`target` (node-typed, not the old flat `xsd:string` `subjectId`/`objectId`) in both directions plus one-hop impact propagation; `graphql.ts` replaced the removed `docId`-scoped block query with `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (bounded-depth nested `root`/`children` selection — GraphQL has no native recursion, so depth is generated explicitly, default 10). `verifyPhase0.ts` was rewritten into a full idempotent, self-cleaning live test of the whole pipeline (AST parsing → track/ingest → GraphQL tree read → `FolderNode` ingestion → `Assertion` CRUD + WOQL traversal → temporal commit management); `npm run verify:phase0 -- --db` and `npm run build` both confirmed passing.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01B",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF000Z",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01C",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Discovered while wiring this up**: TerminusDB enforces referential integrity on document delete — deleting a still-referenced document (e.g. an `ArtifactNode` still listed in a `FolderNode.children`, or a `BlockNode` still pointed to by `ArtifactNode.root`) fails with a `SchemaCheckFailure`, not silently. The best-effort delete helpers in `crud.ts` (`deleteDocumentIfExists`/`deleteDocumentsIfExist`) used to swallow *all* errors on the assumption only \"not found\" could occur — that assumption was wrong and masked this failure mode; they now log instead of swallowing silently, and any caller managing referenced state (like `verifyPhase0.ts`'s cleanup) has to delete in reverse-reference order.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6CR01D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Fixed**: `ArtifactNode` missing `@inherits: [\"BaseNode\"]` in `schema.json` — added, live and verified (`kg:track`/`kg:ingest` run cleanly against it).",
    "title": "00C6Q3P4ER00N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Not yet started",
    "title": "00C6834Z70012",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:47:23.296Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0013",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB0016",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T03:52:24.448Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0014",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB0017",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T03:52:24.448Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0015",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Heading levels don't define tree structure**: `astParser.ts`'s `isStructural` check treats `heading` like any other flat block type, so a document's headings and their following paragraphs/lists all end up as siblings directly under the root, with no nesting by heading level. Confirmed live: a doc with `# Title` / `## Section A` / `## Section B` parses into `Title, (intro), Section A, (para), (list), Section B, ...` all as flat children of \"Document Root,\" not `Title → Section A → (para), (list)`. Lists themselves (ordered and unordered) do nest correctly — `list → listItem → nested list → ...` — this gap is specific to headings. **Must ship before reconciliation matching** (below) goes live — see that entry for why.",
    "title": "00C5FPAHF0015",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-29T01:19:00.916Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0016",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB0019",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T03:52:24.448Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Reconciliation matching for re-ingestion** — **design settled, not yet implemented** (`Aperas-reconciliation-matching-design.md`, `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B/§4.A/§4.B/Appendix G): re-ingesting an already-ingested artifact currently still orphans its entire previous `BlockNode` tree. Design: Gestalt (Ratcliff/Obershelp) tree diff, leaf content anchors containers by context, explicit `tombstonedAt` marker for unmatched nodes (not implicit), covers `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` structural drift as well as within-artifact `BlockNode` content, reports changed/moved as well as added/removed. Surfaced a prerequisite schema fix along the way: `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` move off `Lexical` keying on `path` to Snowflake ids (same as `BlockNode`), `path` becoming a plain mutable field — full rationale in Appendix G. **Blocked on**: heading-nesting (below) must ship first, or the first re-ingest after that fix mass-orphans everything reconciliation was meant to protect.",
    "title": "00C5FPAHF0017",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-29T01:19:00.916Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0018",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001B",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T03:52:24.448Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF0019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF0019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Fractal Ontology Enhancements** (`Aperas-fractal-ontology-implementation-plan.md` Stage 2, items 4-5): AI-driven summarization during ingestion (splitting blocks intelligently into `title` vs `text`) and structural extraction of inline Markdown links into `BaseLink` edges. Confirmed still unimplemented: `astParser.ts`'s `isStructural` node-type list doesn't even include `link`, so inline Markdown links are currently just silently absorbed into the parent block's raw `text`, not extracted at all.",
    "title": "00C5FQW6D0004",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T02:02:24.104Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C5FPAHF001A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C5FPAHF001A",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C64Z9NB001D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T03:52:24.448Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
