    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C5FPAA2006E"
    ],
    "text": "Surface projections reveal the multi-tab reference model (Article, Source, Talk, History) so humans and agents navigate the exact same operational state.",
    "title": "00C6HQACJ0041",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66Q1MC803R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66Q1MC803R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A loadable `SKILL.md` (Agent Skills, per the Open-Source Stack section below) teaching a coding agent when and how to use the `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert` CLI built in Phase 0 — not yet designed.",
    "title": "00C66Q1MC803R",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T04:23:56.893Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66Q271R01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66Q271R01D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Basic Assertion Authoring** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`). New `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert` CLI commands (`kgCli.ts`) let a human or agent actually write and inspect a real `Assertion` — previously the only thing that ever called `insertAssertion` was a hardcoded synthetic edge in `verifyPhase0.ts`'s test harness. `source`/`target` accept either a full node id (direct addressing) or a bare artifact/folder path (addressing from memory, resolved via `getArtifactRecord`/the new `getFolderRecord`, artifact tried first since the two never collide) — block-level assertions stay direct-id-only, since nothing in Phase 0 creates a situation where a human needs to hunt for a block id with no other context, so no \"browse the tree\" command was built. New narrow `deleteAssertion` (`crud.ts`) does exact source/predicate/target deletion, distinct from the existing blunt `deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` (kept for demo/reset cleanup only). Live end-to-end test against two real artifacts (assert → list → unassert → list-empty) surfaced one real bug: WOQL binds a literal-typed field (`predicate`, `xsd:string`) as a wrapped `{\"@type\", \"@value\"}` object rather than a plain string, unlike node-typed `source`/`target` bindings — `kg:assertions` printed `[object Object]` until fixed with an `unwrapLiteral` helper in `woql.ts`'s `queryNodeAssertions`. Never caught by `verifyPhase0.ts`'s existing Assertion test because that only checks binding presence/membership, never a literal field's actual value. Reordered from Phase 2 into Phase 0 itself (not merely Phase 1) per `Aperas-design.md`'s roadmap, so Phase 1 skill-building starts with it already available.",
    "title": "00C66Q271R01D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:21.948Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66Q271R01P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66Q271R01P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Assertion skill(s) (Phase 1)**: a loadable `SKILL.md` teaching a coding agent when/how to use the `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert` CLI (built in Phase 0, above) — not yet designed.",
    "title": "00C6834Z70019",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:47:23.296Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
