  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG002",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG005",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR006",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00J",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00Y",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR014"
    ],
    "title": "# Agentic BFS Projection — Design",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG002",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG003",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG004"
    ],
    "title": "## 0. What this is",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG003",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A names three projection modes. Mode 1 (Artifact\nProjection) is built (`Aperas-artifact-projection-design.md`). Mode 3 — *\"Agentic Interface\n(BFS Traversal): AI agents interact with the graph exactly like the Human UI... receive folded\nviews and can navigate continuously from a workspace root `FolderNode` down to a deeply nested\n`BlockNode` using BFS tool calls to expand subtrees\"* — has been named since early design but\nnever built. This doc is its first concrete implementation: a CLI command that walks the\nfractal tree from any root, showing folded (title-level) structure, bounded by an optional\ndepth.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZG003",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG004",
    "children": [],
    "text": "It surfaced while designing basic assertion authoring (`Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`\n§2) as \"a way to find a block id to assert about\" — but it is not an assertion-only debug\nhelper. It is a general structural browse/overview tool: the query capability this codebase is\ncurrently missing (see §1), independently useful for exploring the KG regardless of whether an\nassertion follows.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZG004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG006",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG007",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR005"
    ],
    "title": "## 1. Addressing is direct-or-query, not \"memory\"",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Node addressing is either **direct** (you already hold a real id in your current context —\nhowever it got there: a prior command's output, a query result, an agent's own conversation\nhistory) or **query-based** (you don't have an id, so you use a tool that finds one). What\nthis codebase actually has, audited:",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZG006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG007",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG008",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR001",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR003"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C66ZPNZG007",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZG008",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR000"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZG008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR000",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Exact-field lookup** — `getArtifactRecord`/`getFolderRecord` (`artifacts.ts`/`folders.ts`),\n  an equality match on the `path` field. This is what `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert`\n  already use for artifact/folder addressing (`Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md` §2) —\n  it was previously described as \"from memory,\" which conflated a trivial query with a distinct\n  human-recall mechanism. It's just a query, the simplest kind.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR000",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR002"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**WOQL pattern queries** — `queryNodeAssertions`/`traceImpactPropagation` (`woql.ts`), over\n  `Assertion` edges only.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR003",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR004"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR004",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Bounded-depth nested-tree reads** — `getArtifactTreeViaGraphQL` (`graphql.ts`), one\n  `ArtifactNode` at a time.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR005",
    "children": [],
    "text": "None of these do **content search** — there is no \"find the node whose text/title contains X\"\ncapability anywhere in this codebase today. This design does not add one either; it adds\n**structural** browsing (by position and folded label), which is a different, narrower thing.\nContent search remains a real, unfilled gap — out of scope here, not solved by omission.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR005",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR006",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR007",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR008",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR009"
    ],
    "title": "## 2. Render rule: the title-fallback gap",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR007",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`FolderNode.title`/`ArtifactNode.title` are always meaningful (dirname/filename). `BlockNode`\nis not so simple: per `astParser.ts`'s `convertAstNode`, `title` is only ever set to something\nreal for `heading` (the raw heading line) and the synthetic `root` (`\"Document Root\"`) — every\nother type (`paragraph`, `code`, `list`, `listItem`, `blockquote`) falls back to the block's own\n`blockId` as its `title` (`astParser.ts:76`, \"to be replaced by AI agent in the future\" — that\nenhancement is still unbuilt, `Aperas-dev-status.md` \"Not yet started\"). A naive title-only tree\nwould print a raw id for 5 of 6 block types.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Fallback rule, per node:",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR009",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00A",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00C",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00E",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00G"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR009",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00B"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode`: always `title`.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00B",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00D"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`BlockNode` whose `title !== blockId` (i.e. `heading`/`root`): `title`.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00F"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`BlockNode` with real `text` but a fallback title (`paragraph`/`code`): first line of `text`,\n  trimmed.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00H"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`BlockNode` with neither (`list`/`listItem`/`blockquote` — deliberately content-empty per the\n  container-text-purity design, `Aperas-dev-status.md`'s \"Heading levels now define tree\n  structure\" entry): show just `[type]`, no excerpt — the real content is one level deeper, in\n  children.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00K"
    ],
    "title": "## 3. Command: `kg:tree [path] [--depth N]`",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00M",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00P",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00R",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00T",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00W"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00K",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00N"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`path` optional, defaults to `.` (the artifacts-root `FolderNode`) — \"the full tree from\n  folders.\"",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00P",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00Q"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Same addressing as the assertion CLI: a full node id or a bare artifact/folder path, resolved\n  via the existing `resolveNodeRef` (direct-or-query, §1).",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00S"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "No depth limit by default — genuinely the full tree. `--depth N` truncates to N levels,\n  printing a `…` marker at each truncation point rather than silently stopping, so it's visibly\n  a limit, not the actual leaf.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00T",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00V"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "One recursive walk handles every level uniformly — `FolderNode` (nested `FolderNode`s,\n  `ArtifactNode` references, README-derived `BlockNode` children) and `ArtifactNode` →\n  `BlockNode` tree alike, since the fractal ontology means no node kind needs special-casing\n  beyond §2's render rule.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00X"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Output: one line per node, indented by depth: `<id>  [<kind>]  <label>` — `<kind>` is\n  `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` for those, or the `BlockNode`'s own mdast `type` for blocks;\n  `<label>` per §2.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00Z"
    ],
    "title": "## 4. Relationship to other projections",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR00Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR010",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR012"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR00Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR010",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR011"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR010",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Artifact Projection** (`kg:project`) always fully unfolds one artifact back to clean\n  Markdown — this mode is deliberately folded (titles, not full text), spans the whole KG from\n  any root, and exists to browse/locate, not to regenerate a file. Different jobs.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR011",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR012",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR013"
    ],
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR012",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Assertion CLI** (`kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert`) — this closes the block-level\n  addressing gap that design doc flagged as deliberately unsolved (\"nothing in Phase 0 creates\n  a situation where a human needs to hunt for a block id with no other context... so no 'browse\n  the tree' command was built\"). That reasoning is superseded now that a real need (this one)\n  exists; `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md` §2 should cross-reference this doc instead.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR013",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR014",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR015"
    ],
    "title": "## 5. Phase placement (proposed, not yet decided)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPNZR015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPNZR015",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`Aperas-dev-status.md` currently lists the Agentic BFS interface as a Phase 1 item, undesigned.\nGiven the same reasoning that pulled Artifact Projection's assertion-authoring gap into Phase 0\n(a real capability gap blocking basic KG usability, not contingent on the UI existing first),\nthis is proposed for Phase 0 too — but unlike the earlier two moves, this one hasn't been\nexplicitly confirmed yet.",
    "title": "00C66ZPNZR015",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPRQG00C",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00D",
      "BlockNode/00C67F1KB800J"
    ],
    "title": "## 2. Addressing is direct-or-query, not \"resolution\" or \"memory\"",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPRQG00D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00E",
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00G"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C67F1KB800D",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPRQG00E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00F"
    ],
    "title": "00C67F1KB800E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPRQG00F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Direct addressing** — the normal case. You already hold a real node id, from wherever (a\n  prior command's own printed confirmation, a query result, code that still has the parsed\n  tree available). `AssertionInput.source`/`target` (`BlockNode/<id>`, `ArtifactNode/<id>`,\n  `FolderNode/<id>`) is passed through completely unchanged — no lookup, no search, nothing to\n  resolve.",
    "title": "00C67F1KB800F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPRQG00G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C67F1KB800H"
    ],
    "title": "00C67F1KB800G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPRQG00H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Query-based addressing** — applies when there's no id in hand at all. The simplest query\n  this project has is an exact match on a path, and both path-addressable node kinds get it\n  identically: a bare artifact path (e.g. `Aperas-design.md`) resolves via the existing\n  `getArtifactRecord` (`artifacts.ts`) to `ArtifactNode/<artifactId>`, and a bare folder path\n  (e.g. `.` for the artifacts root, or a subdirectory name) resolves via the structurally\n  identical `getFolderRecord` (`folders.ts`) to `FolderNode/<folderId>`. An artifact path and a\n  folder path never collide, so trying artifact-then-folder resolution in that order is\n  unambiguous. (Earlier revisions of this doc called this \"from memory\" — that framing\n  conflated an ordinary exact-match query with a distinct human-recall mechanism; see\n  `Aperas-agentic-bfs-projection-design.md` §1 for the fuller correction and the complete\n  inventory of what query tools this project actually has.)",
    "title": "00C66ZPRQG00H",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T04:57:26.702Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPRQG00J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`BlockNode` has no path-like shortcut: nobody carries an opaque id in their head or types block\ncontent as a handle. So a block-level assertion needs either an id already in hand from\nwhatever produced the claim (e.g. a skill that just parsed content and still holds the tree), or\na real query tool to find one — see `Aperas-agentic-bfs-projection-design.md` (`kg:tree`), which\nwalks the fractal tree from any root and closes this gap. (Superseded reasoning, kept for\ncontext: this doc originally argued no such command was needed in Phase 0, since nothing yet\ncreated a situation requiring one — that held until the tree-view idea was recognized as a\ngeneral-purpose query tool in its own right, not just an assertion helper.)",
    "title": "00C66ZPRQG00J",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T04:57:26.702Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPRQG00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPRQG00P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`kg:assert <source> <predicate> <target>` — `source`/`target` each accept a full node id\n  (direct addressing) or a bare artifact/folder path (query-based addressing, per §2); calls\n  `insertAssertion`.",
    "title": "00C67F1KB800P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPXPR00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPXPR00Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Assertion skill(s)",
    "title": "00C6HQACJ003K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPXPR012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPXPR012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A loadable `SKILL.md` (Agent Skills, per the Open-Source Stack section below) teaching a coding agent when and how to use the `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert` CLI built in Phase 0 — not yet designed.",
    "title": "00C6HQACJ003P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPXPR018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPXPR018",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C66ZPXPR019"
    ],
    "text": "Renders continuous Markdown outliner trees directly from TerminusDB AST nodes.",
    "title": "00C6HQACJ003W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C66ZPXPR019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C66ZPXPR019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Renders continuous Markdown outliner trees directly from TerminusDB AST nodes.",
    "title": "00C6HQACJ003X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER002",
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER004",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00B",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00R",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G016",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G01M",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G01Y"
    ],
    "text": "`Aperas-agentic-bfs-projection-design.md` conflated two different traversal shapes under one\nwrong name — a depth-bounded recursive walk it called \"BFS Traversal\" is actually depth-first\n(IDDFS-shaped, once bounded), not breadth-first. This doc replaces it: three distinct tools,\ncorrectly named, plus a third capability (keyword/regex search) every earlier revision flagged\nas missing but never built. Together they answer \"what does an agent or human have to find a\nnode or explore the graph,\" per `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A's Agentic Interface\nconcept and the gap first identified in `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md` §2.",
    "title": "# Agentic Query Tools — Design",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER002",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER003"
    ],
    "text": "`Aperas-agentic-bfs-projection-design.md` conflated two different traversal shapes under one\nwrong name — a depth-bounded recursive walk it called \"BFS Traversal\" is actually depth-first\n(IDDFS-shaped, once bounded), not breadth-first. This doc replaces it: three distinct tools,\ncorrectly named, plus a third capability (keyword/regex search) every earlier revision flagged\nas missing but never built. Together they answer \"what does an agent or human have to find a\nnode or explore the graph,\" per `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A's Agentic Interface\nconcept and the gap first identified in `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md` §2.",
    "title": "## 0. What this is, and what it supersedes",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER003",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`Aperas-agentic-bfs-projection-design.md` conflated two different traversal shapes under one\nwrong name — a depth-bounded recursive walk it called \"BFS Traversal\" is actually depth-first\n(IDDFS-shaped, once bounded), not breadth-first. This doc replaces it: three distinct tools,\ncorrectly named, plus a third capability (keyword/regex search) every earlier revision flagged\nas missing but never built. Together they answer \"what does an agent or human have to find a\nnode or explore the graph,\" per `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A's Agentic Interface\nconcept and the gap first identified in `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md` §2.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER004",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER005"
    ],
    "text": "**`kg:tree`** — a deep structural map: recursively lists nodes across many levels, optionally\n  depth-bounded. Algorithmically a depth-first walk with an optional depth cutoff —\n  IDDFS-shaped, not BFS. Good for getting oriented across a large chunk of the KG at a glance.",
    "title": "## 1. Three distinct tools, not one",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER005",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER006",
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER008",
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00A"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C6833Y6G004",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER006",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER007"
    ],
    "text": "**`kg:tree`** — a deep structural map: recursively lists nodes across many levels, optionally\n  depth-bounded. Algorithmically a depth-first walk with an optional depth cutoff —\n  IDDFS-shaped, not BFS. Good for getting oriented across a large chunk of the KG at a glance.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER007",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`kg:tree`** — a deep structural map: recursively lists nodes across many levels, optionally\n  depth-bounded. Algorithmically a depth-first walk with an optional depth cutoff —\n  IDDFS-shaped, not BFS. Good for getting oriented across a large chunk of the KG at a glance.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G006",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER008",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G008"
    ],
    "text": "**`kg:unfold`** (and its inverse, `kg:fold`) — true breadth-first: given one node, show its\n  own `title` plus the full `text` of each of its immediate children (first level only) — no\n  recursion, no depth param, since \"first level\" is the whole point. Named `fold`/`unfold` (not\n  `collapse`/`expand`) to match the ontology's own existing vocabulary — see §3, this is also\n  the first thing to ever give the long-inert `BlockNode.unfolded` schema field a real effect.\n  This is the real analog of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A mode 3's \"BFS tool calls to\n  expand subtrees\": a single frontier-expansion step an agent calls repeatedly, choosing which\n  child to unfold next based on what it just read.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER009",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`kg:expand`** — true breadth-first: given one node, show the full `text` of each of its\n  immediate children (first level only) — no recursion, no depth param, since \"first level\" is\n  the whole point. This is the real analog of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A mode 3's\n  \"BFS tool calls to expand subtrees\": a single frontier-expansion step an agent calls\n  repeatedly, choosing which child to expand next based on what it just read.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER009",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00B"
    ],
    "text": "**`kg:search`** — keyword/regex content search, matched server-side via WOQL. Not structural\n  at all — finds nodes by matching a pattern against content, regardless of position in the\n  tree. Closes the gap every earlier revision of this design named and left open.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`kg:search`** — keyword/regex content search, matched server-side via WOQL. Not structural\n  at all — finds nodes by matching a pattern against content, regardless of position in the\n  tree. Closes the gap every earlier revision of this design named and left open.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00C",
    "children": [],
    "title": "## 2. `kg:tree` — render rule: `title`, exclusively",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "An earlier revision proposed falling back to a text excerpt when `title` isn't meaningful.\nRejected: a `BlockNode`'s `title` literally *is* its own `blockId` whenever nothing has\nsummarized it yet (`astParser.ts:76`) — and that **is** the meaningful signal, not a gap to\npaper over. Seeing a raw id as a node's title tells the reader \"this node is opaque — nothing\nhas read and summarized me\" (Fractal Ontology Enhancements' AI-summarization step, still\nunbuilt per `Aperas-dev-status.md`). Extracting a text excerpt instead would hide that signal\nbehind a false sense of readability. So: print `title` uniformly for every node kind, no\nfallback branching, no special-casing for containers either — `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode`\ntitles are always meaningful (dirname/filename) anyway, so the rule is genuinely uniform.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Command: `kg:tree [path] [--depth N]`",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00E",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00F",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00F",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00G",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00G",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`path` optional, defaults to `.` (the artifacts-root `FolderNode`) — the full tree from\n  folders.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00H",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00J",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00J",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Same addressing as the assertion CLI: a full node id or a bare artifact/folder path, resolved\n  via the existing `resolveNodeRef` (direct-or-query, `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`\n  §2).",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00K",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00M",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00M",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "No depth limit by default — genuinely the full tree. `--depth N` truncates to N levels,\n  printing a `…` marker at each truncation point rather than silently stopping, so it's visibly\n  a limit, not the actual leaf.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00N",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00P",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00P",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "One recursive walk handles every level uniformly — `FolderNode` (nested `FolderNode`s,\n  `ArtifactNode` references, README-derived `BlockNode` children) and `ArtifactNode` →\n  `BlockNode` tree alike; the fractal ontology means no node kind needs special-casing.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00Q",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00R",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00R",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Output: one line per node, indented by depth: `<id>  [<kind>]  <title>` — `<kind>` is\n  `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` for those, or the `BlockNode`'s own mdast `type` for blocks.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00S",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00T",
    "children": [],
    "title": "## 3. `kg:expand` — one breadth-first step",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Command: `kg:expand <path>`",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00V",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00W",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00W",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00X",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00X",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`path`: same direct-or-query addressing as everywhere else (full id or artifact/folder path).",
    "title": "00C67F1GER00Y",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER00Z",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER00Z",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "No depth, no recursion by design — resolves to one node, then for each of its immediate\n  children prints `<id>  [<kind>]  <full text>`. Full `text`, not `title` — the opposite bias\n  from `kg:tree`, since the whole point of expanding is finally reading real content, not\n  another folded label.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER010",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER011",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER011",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A child with no `text` of its own (a container — `list`/`listItem`/`blockquote`, or a\n  `heading` whose real content lives in *its* children, not itself) prints\n  `<id>  [<kind>]  (no text of its own — see kg:expand <id>)`, since there's nothing to surface\n  by looking harder at that node — only by expanding one level further.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER012",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER013",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER013",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER014",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Composable with `kg:tree`: `kg:tree` gives the map, `kg:expand` gives the read at any point\n  on it — the two together are the \"BFS tool calls to expand subtrees\" workflow\n  `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A describes, made concrete.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER014",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER015",
    "children": [],
    "title": "## 4. `kg:search` — keyword/regex content search",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER016",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Command: `kg:search <pattern>` — PCRE-style regex, matching `WOQL.re`'s own semantics.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER016",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Confirmed live (not just documented): TerminusDB's WOQL builder exposes\n`WOQL.re(pattern, inputVarName, resultVarList)` (`terminusdb` npm package, `lib/woql.js:1262`)\n— genuine server-side regex matching, not a client-side scan. Tested directly against the real\nKG: `WOQL.re('Assertion', titleVar, matchVar)` combined with `WOQL.triple(doc, 'title',\ntitleVar)` correctly matched 3 real `BlockNode` titles containing \"Assertion.\" A pattern with a\nregex metacharacter (`kg:\\w+`) also matched correctly using ordinary single-level JS string\nescaping — the \"escape twice\" note in the client's own docstring turned out to be about\ninternal JSON-LD wire transport, already handled by the client library; callers don't need to\ndouble-escape anything themselves.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER017",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER018",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER018",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER019",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER019",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER01A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER01A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Searches `title` and `text` across all three node classes (`BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode`,\n  `FolderNode`) — six queries (3 classes × 2 fields), each\n  `WOQL.and(WOQL.triple(v.Doc, field, v.Value), WOQL.re(pattern, v.Value, v.Match))`. A\n  class/field a given document doesn't have (e.g. `Optional text` absent) simply produces no\n  triple to match against — no special-casing needed.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER01A",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER01B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER01B",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER01B",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER01C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER01C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`title`/`text` are `xsd:string` literals, so bindings come back wrapped\n  (`{\"@type\", \"@value\"}`), exactly like `predicate` did in `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`\n  §4 — reuses the existing `unwrapLiteral` (`woql.ts`) rather than re-solving the same problem.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER01C",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER01D",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C67F1GER01D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER01E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER01E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Output: `<id>  [<kind>]  <field>  <value>` per match, across all six queries, deduplicated by\n  id (a node could match on both `title` and `text`).",
    "title": "00C67F1GER01E",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER01F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER01F",
    "children": [],
    "title": "## 5. Phase placement",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1GER01G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1GER01G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`Aperas-dev-status.md` currently lists the Agentic BFS interface as an undesigned Phase 1 item.\nCarried over from the prior revision, still just a proposal, not a decision: given the same\nreasoning that pulled Artifact Projection and Basic Assertion Authoring into Phase 0 (a real\ncapability gap blocking basic KG usability, not contingent on the UI existing first), all three\ntools here are proposed for Phase 0 too.",
    "title": "00C67F1GER01G",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T05:41:17.722Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1KB800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1KB800H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Query-based addressing** — applies when there's no id in hand at all. The simplest query\n  this project has is an exact match on a path, and both path-addressable node kinds get it\n  identically: a bare artifact path (e.g. `Aperas-design.md`) resolves via the existing\n  `getArtifactRecord` (`artifacts.ts`) to `ArtifactNode/<artifactId>`, and a bare folder path\n  (e.g. `.` for the artifacts root, or a subdirectory name) resolves via the structurally\n  identical `getFolderRecord` (`folders.ts`) to `FolderNode/<folderId>`. An artifact path and a\n  folder path never collide, so trying artifact-then-folder resolution in that order is\n  unambiguous. (Earlier revisions of this doc called this \"from memory\" — that framing\n  conflated an ordinary exact-match query with a distinct human-recall mechanism; see\n  `Aperas-agentic-query-tools-design.md` §1 for the fuller correction and the complete\n  inventory of what query tools this project actually has.)",
    "title": "00C67F1KB800H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C67F1KB800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C67F1KB800J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`BlockNode` has no path-like shortcut: nobody carries an opaque id in their head or types block\ncontent as a handle. So a block-level assertion needs either an id already in hand from\nwhatever produced the claim (e.g. a skill that just parsed content and still holds the tree), or\na real query tool to find one — see `Aperas-agentic-query-tools-design.md` (`kg:tree`,\n`kg:expand`, `kg:search`), which closes this gap three ways: a structural map, a one-level\ncontent peek, and keyword/regex search. (Superseded reasoning, kept for context: this doc\noriginally argued no such command was needed in Phase 0, since nothing yet created a situation\nrequiring one — that held until the need was recognized as a set of general-purpose query\ntools in their own right, not just an assertion helper.)",
    "title": "00C67F1KB800J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G008",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`kg:unfold`** (and its inverse, `kg:fold`) — true breadth-first: given one node, show its\n  own `title` plus the full `text` of each of its immediate children (first level only) — no\n  recursion, no depth param, since \"first level\" is the whole point. Named `fold`/`unfold` (not\n  `collapse`/`expand`) to match the ontology's own existing vocabulary — see §3, this is also\n  the first thing to ever give the long-inert `BlockNode.unfolded` schema field a real effect.\n  This is the real analog of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A mode 3's \"BFS tool calls to\n  expand subtrees\": a single frontier-expansion step an agent calls repeatedly, choosing which\n  child to unfold next based on what it just read.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G008",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00B",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00C",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00D",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00P",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00Q"
    ],
    "text": "Designing `kg:unfold` (§3) exposed a missed gap in already-shipped ingestion behavior, not just\na display-layer choice: `heading` and `blockquote`/`listItem` were all being treated as\nequally content-less containers (`text = \"\"`), but they aren't equally opaque —",
    "title": "## 2. A real implementation gap this surfaced, fixed directly in `astParser.ts`",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Designing `kg:unfold` (§3) exposed a missed gap in already-shipped ingestion behavior, not just\na display-layer choice: `heading` and `blockquote`/`listItem` were all being treated as\nequally content-less containers (`text = \"\"`), but they aren't equally opaque —",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00E",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00G",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00J",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00M"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00D",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00E",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00F"
    ],
    "text": "A `heading`'s real content lives in its children, but per the folding philosophy (\"a block's\n  children fold into its text (abstract)\"), it should still carry an abstract of its own, the\n  same way `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` already do via `extractAbstract`. It didn't — it was\n  hardcoded to `\"\"` regardless.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A `heading`'s real content lives in its children, but per the folding philosophy (\"a block's\n  children fold into its text (abstract)\"), it should still carry an abstract of its own, the\n  same way `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` already do via `extractAbstract`. It didn't — it was\n  hardcoded to `\"\"` regardless.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00F",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00G",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00H"
    ],
    "text": "A `listItem` is a real semantic unit (like a heading's section, just one level down), so it\n  deserves the same treatment — also missing.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A `listItem` is a real semantic unit (like a heading's section, just one level down), so it\n  deserves the same treatment — also missing.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00K"
    ],
    "text": "A `list` genuinely has no content of its own — its children (`listItem`s) are the actual\n  content units. It's the *only* true content-less container.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A `list` genuinely has no content of its own — its children (`listItem`s) are the actual\n  content units. It's the *only* true content-less container.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00K",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00M",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00N"
    ],
    "text": "A `blockquote` is a quote, not a summary — its full content should be projected as-is, not\n  reduced to an abstract or emptied out.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "A `blockquote` is a quote, not a summary — its full content should be projected as-is, not\n  reduced to an abstract or emptied out.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Fixed in `astParser.ts`'s `convertAstNode`: `heading`/`listItem` now compute `text` via\n`extractAbstract` once their `children` exist (the first paragraph found among descendants,\ncascading correctly through nesting — confirmed live: a `Sub` heading two levels down correctly\npicked up its own nearest paragraph, not an ancestor's); `list` still empties `text`; `blockquote`\nnow falls through to the ordinary leaf default (`text = rawText`, its full raw slice, quote\nmarkers included) instead of being emptied. Verified this doesn't disturb reconciliation:\n`reconcile.ts` keeps its own independent `LEAF_TYPES`/`CONTAINER_TYPES` (type-based, not\ntext-based) for Stage A/B matching, so none of this changes which nodes match how — confirmed by\nre-running `verify:phase0 -- --db` clean, both in-memory and against the live DB.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Known limitation surfaced by this fix**: `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` skip re-ingestion based on file\ncontent hash — a parser-logic change like this one doesn't change any file's bytes, so already-\ningested real artifacts keep their old (empty) heading/listItem `text` until something forces\nre-ingestion. Confirmed live: re-running `kg:track`/`kg:ingest` after this fix touched zero\nartifacts. Not fixed here — a real, pre-existing gap (parser version isn't part of the\nchange-detection key), out of scope for this design.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00S",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00T",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00V"
    ],
    "text": "An earlier revision proposed falling back to a text excerpt when `title` isn't meaningful.\nRejected: a `BlockNode`'s `title` literally *is* its own `blockId` whenever nothing has\nsummarized it yet (`astParser.ts:76`) — and that **is** the meaningful signal, not a gap to\npaper over. Seeing a raw id as a node's title tells the reader \"this node is opaque — nothing\nhas read and summarized me\" (Fractal Ontology Enhancements' AI-summarization step, still\nunbuilt per `Aperas-dev-status.md`). Extracting a text excerpt instead would hide that signal\nbehind a false sense of readability. So: print `title` uniformly for every node kind, no\nfallback branching, no special-casing for containers either — `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode`\ntitles are always meaningful (dirname/filename) anyway, so the rule is genuinely uniform.",
    "title": "## 3. `kg:tree` — render rule: `title`, exclusively",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "An earlier revision proposed falling back to a text excerpt when `title` isn't meaningful.\nRejected: a `BlockNode`'s `title` literally *is* its own `blockId` whenever nothing has\nsummarized it yet (`astParser.ts:76`) — and that **is** the meaningful signal, not a gap to\npaper over. Seeing a raw id as a node's title tells the reader \"this node is opaque — nothing\nhas read and summarized me\" (Fractal Ontology Enhancements' AI-summarization step, still\nunbuilt per `Aperas-dev-status.md`). Extracting a text excerpt instead would hide that signal\nbehind a false sense of readability. So: print `title` uniformly for every node kind, no\nfallback branching, no special-casing for containers either — `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode`\ntitles are always meaningful (dirname/filename) anyway, so the rule is genuinely uniform.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Command: `kg:tree [path] [--depth N]`",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00T",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00V",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00W",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00Y",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G010",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G012",
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G014"
    ],
    "ordered": false,
    "start": 1,
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00V",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00W",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00X"
    ],
    "text": "`path` optional, defaults to `.` (the artifacts-root `FolderNode`) — the full tree from\n  folders.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`path` optional, defaults to `.` (the artifacts-root `FolderNode`) — the full tree from\n  folders.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00X",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00Z"
    ],
    "text": "Same addressing as the assertion CLI: a full node id or a bare artifact/folder path, resolved\n  via the existing `resolveNodeRef` (direct-or-query, `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`\n  §2).",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G00Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Same addressing as the assertion CLI: a full node id or a bare artifact/folder path, resolved\n  via the existing `resolveNodeRef` (direct-or-query, `Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`\n  §2).",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G00Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G010",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G011"
    ],
    "text": "No depth limit by default — genuinely the full tree. `--depth N` truncates to N levels,\n  printing a `…` marker at each truncation point rather than silently stopping, so it's visibly\n  a limit, not the actual leaf.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G010",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "No depth limit by default — genuinely the full tree. `--depth N` truncates to N levels,\n  printing a `…` marker at each truncation point rather than silently stopping, so it's visibly\n  a limit, not the actual leaf.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G011",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G012",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G013"
    ],
    "text": "One recursive walk handles every level uniformly — `FolderNode` (nested `FolderNode`s,\n  `ArtifactNode` references, README-derived `BlockNode` children) and `ArtifactNode` →\n  `BlockNode` tree alike; the fractal ontology means no node kind needs special-casing.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G012",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "One recursive walk handles every level uniformly — `FolderNode` (nested `FolderNode`s,\n  `ArtifactNode` references, README-derived `BlockNode` children) and `ArtifactNode` →\n  `BlockNode` tree alike; the fractal ontology means no node kind needs special-casing.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G013",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6833Y6G014",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G015"
    ],
    "text": "Output: one line per node, indented by depth: `<id>  [<kind>]  <title>` — `<kind>` is\n  `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` for those, or the `BlockNode`'s own mdast `type` for blocks.",
    "title": "00C6833Y6G014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6833Y6G015",
