  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6834Z7000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6834Z7000Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Basic Assertion Authoring** — **implemented and live-verified** (`Aperas-basic-assertion-skill-design.md`). New `kg:assert`/`kg:assertions`/`kg:unassert` CLI commands (`kgCli.ts`) let a human or agent actually write and inspect a real `Assertion` — previously the only thing that ever called `insertAssertion` was a hardcoded synthetic edge in `verifyPhase0.ts`'s test harness. `source`/`target` accept either a full node id (direct addressing) or a bare artifact/folder path (query-based addressing, resolved via `getArtifactRecord`/the new `getFolderRecord`, artifact tried first since the two never collide) — block-level assertions stay direct-id-only; closing that gap became its own effort, see \"Agentic Query Tools\" below. New narrow `deleteAssertion` (`crud.ts`) does exact source/predicate/target deletion, distinct from the existing blunt `deleteAssertionsInvolvingNode` (kept for demo/reset cleanup only). Live end-to-end test against two real artifacts (assert → list → unassert → list-empty) surfaced one real bug: WOQL binds a literal-typed field (`predicate`, `xsd:string`) as a wrapped `{\"@type\", \"@value\"}` object rather than a plain string, unlike node-typed `source`/`target` bindings — `kg:assertions` printed `[object Object]` until fixed with an `unwrapLiteral` helper in `woql.ts`'s `queryNodeAssertions`. Never caught by `verifyPhase0.ts`'s existing Assertion test because that only checks binding presence/membership, never a literal field's actual value. Reordered from Phase 2 into Phase 0 itself (not merely Phase 1) per `Aperas-design.md`'s roadmap, so Phase 1 skill-building starts with it already available.",
    "title": "00C6834Z7000Y",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:47:23.296Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6834Z7000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6834Z7000Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Agentic Query Tools** — reordered from Phase 1 into Phase 0, design settled (`Aperas-agentic-query-tools-design.md`), not yet implemented. Three CLI tools closing the block-level addressing gap Basic Assertion Authoring (above) left open, and making mode 3 of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A concrete for the first time: `kg:tree` (a deep, title-only structural map — depth-first with an optional depth bound, corrected from an earlier revision that mislabeled this \"BFS\"), `kg:unfold`/`kg:fold` (the actual breadth-first primitive: one level, full content, the first code to ever give the long-inert `BlockNode.unfolded` flag a real effect), and `kg:search` (keyword/regex content search via `WOQL.re`, confirmed live against the real KG). Designing this also surfaced and fixed a real gap in already-shipped ingestion: `heading`/`listItem` now get a real abstract (`extractAbstract`, cascading correctly through nesting) instead of a hardcoded empty `text`, and `blockquote` now projects its full content instead of being emptied like a true container — only `list` still has none. Fixed directly in `astParser.ts`, verified via `verify:phase0 -- --db` (clean, no regression — reconciliation's own matching is type-based, not text-based, so unaffected); note already-ingested real artifacts won't pick up the new text until something forces re-ingestion, since `kg:track`'s hash-based skip doesn't know the parser itself changed.",
    "title": "00C6834Z7000Z",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:47:23.296Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6834Z70010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6834Z70010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Agentic Query Tools** — reordered from Phase 1 into Phase 0, design settled (`Aperas-agentic-query-tools-design.md`), not yet implemented. Three CLI tools closing the block-level addressing gap Basic Assertion Authoring (above) left open, and making mode 3 of `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §5.A concrete for the first time: `kg:tree` (a deep, title-only structural map — depth-first with an optional depth bound, corrected from an earlier revision that mislabeled this \"BFS\"), `kg:unfold`/`kg:fold` (the actual breadth-first primitive: one level, full content, the first code to ever give the long-inert `BlockNode.unfolded` flag a real effect), and `kg:search` (keyword/regex content search via `WOQL.re`, confirmed live against the real KG). Designing this also surfaced and fixed a real gap in already-shipped ingestion: `heading`/`listItem` now get a real abstract (`extractAbstract`, cascading correctly through nesting) instead of a hardcoded empty `text`, and `blockquote` now projects its full content instead of being emptied like a true container — only `list` still has none. Fixed directly in `astParser.ts`, verified via `verify:phase0 -- --db` (clean, no regression — reconciliation's own matching is type-based, not text-based, so unaffected); note already-ingested real artifacts won't pick up the new text until something forces re-ingestion, since `kg:track`'s hash-based skip doesn't know the parser itself changed.",
    "title": "00C6834Z70010",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:47:23.296Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
