  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG010",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Inline features (strikethrough, bold, italic, footnotes, links, ...) are decided out of\n  scope, deliberately confirmed.** None of these are block-level; none go in `isStructural`;\n  none get special-cased. They stay exactly as-is — raw-slice content inside whatever leaf\n  contains them, same as today. Inline structural extraction (addressable spans, extracted\n  links) is the separately-tracked, unbuilt \"Fractal Ontology Enhancements\" item — a different\n  concern from this doc's block/container mapping, not a gap in it.",
    "title": "00C6KAEKM800Z",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T19:00:03.507Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Inline features (strikethrough, bold, italic, footnotes, links, ...) are decided out of\n  scope, deliberately confirmed.** None of these are block-level; none go in `isStructural`;\n  none get special-cased. They stay exactly as-is — raw-slice content inside whatever leaf\n  contains them, same as today. Inline structural extraction (addressable spans, extracted\n  links) is the separately-tracked, unbuilt \"Fractal Ontology Enhancements\" item — a different\n  concern from this doc's block/container mapping, not a gap in it.",
    "title": "00C6KAEKM800Y",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T19:00:03.507Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**YAML frontmatter — parsing shape confirmed, stage-appropriate design settled.**\n  See §5.",
    "title": "00C6JRYTMG012",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T18:36:24.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Confirmed parsing shape**: `remark-frontmatter` (now installed, tested, not yet wired into\n`astParser.ts`) with `.use(remarkFrontmatter, ['yaml'])` recognizes a leading `---\\n...\\n---`\nblock as its own mdast node, `{ type: 'yaml', value: '<raw yaml body, delimiters stripped>' }` —\nconfirmed live against a real multi-key example. Critically, this only *isolates* the block; it\ndoes **not** parse the YAML into an object — `.value` is still just a string (e.g.\n`\"title: My Doc\\ntags: [foo, bar]\\ndraft: true\"`). Turning that into real key/value data needs a\nYAML parser too (e.g. the `yaml` or `js-yaml` package — neither installed yet).",
    "title": "## 5. YAML frontmatter as `ArtifactNode` props — opaque for now, extensible later",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:17:46.661Z",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG014",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Confirmed parsing shape**: `remark-frontmatter` (now installed, tested, not yet wired into\n`astParser.ts`) with `.use(remarkFrontmatter, ['yaml'])` recognizes a leading `---\\n...\\n---`\nblock as its own mdast node, `{ type: 'yaml', value: '<raw yaml body, delimiters stripped>' }` —\nconfirmed live against a real multi-key example. Critically, this only *isolates* the block; it\ndoes **not** parse the YAML into an object — `.value` is still just a string (e.g.\n`\"title: My Doc\\ntags: [foo, bar]\\ndraft: true\"`). Turning that into real key/value data needs a\nYAML parser too (e.g. the `yaml` or `js-yaml` package — neither installed yet).",
    "title": "00C6MH0GCG016",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:17:46.661Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG015",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Shape of the change, not yet built**:",
    "title": "00C6MH0GCG017",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:17:46.661Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG016",
    "children": [],
    "title": "00C6MH0GCG018",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:17:46.661Z",
    "type": "list",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG017",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Frontmatter is file-level metadata, not a block — it should never become a `BlockNode` at all\n  (parallel to how `folders.ts` already treats a directory's own `README.md` specially, never\n  exposing it as a separate `ArtifactNode`). `parseMarkdownTree`'s signature would need to\n  change: return the parsed props alongside the root `BlockNode`, not fold them into the tree.\n  That ripples into every caller (`artifacts.ts`'s `ingestArtifact`, `verifyPhase0.ts`).",
    "title": "00C6MH0GCG019",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:17:46.661Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG018",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Frontmatter is file-level metadata, not a block — it should never become a `BlockNode` at all\n  (parallel to how `folders.ts` already treats a directory's own `README.md` specially, never\n  exposing it as a separate `ArtifactNode`). `parseMarkdownTree`'s signature would need to\n  change: return the parsed props alongside the root `BlockNode`, not fold them into the tree.\n  That ripples into every caller (`artifacts.ts`'s `ingestArtifact`, `verifyPhase0.ts`).",
    "title": "00C6MH0GCG01A",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:17:46.661Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG019",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Realized through §7's unified `props` mechanism, not a bespoke `ArtifactNode.props` field.**\n  An earlier revision of this doc proposed a dedicated `ArtifactNode.props: Optional xsd:string`\n  field specifically for frontmatter. Superseded: §7 designs one generic `props` mechanism for\n  *any* node kind's extensible metadata, and frontmatter is simply one more user of it — a\n  single entry (e.g. `{key: \"frontmatter\", value: \"<raw yaml body, as-is>\"}`) in an\n  `ArtifactNode`'s own `props` list, not a field of its own. Still opaque for this stage (the raw\n  body, not JSON-parsed — no YAML-parsing dependency needed yet), same reasoning as before, just\n  expressed through the shared mechanism instead of a one-off field.",
    "title": "00C6MH0GCG01B",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T20:17:46.661Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG01A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG01A",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Decided: one opaque field for now, not a schema-level key/value store.** Frontmatter\n  keys/values are inherently open-ended (whatever an author writes) — a prior revision of this\n  doc framed this as a choice between one opaque `ArtifactNode.props: Optional xsd:string`\n  (simple, matches existing precedent, but unqueryable) versus graph-native `{key, value}`\n  subdocuments (queryable, but real values aren't uniformly strings — `tags` is a list, `draft`\n  is a boolean — so it needs its own serialization/typing convention). Settled: for this stage,\n  the opaque field — `ArtifactNode.props: Optional xsd:string`, holding the raw frontmatter body\n  as-is (not even JSON-serialized; no YAML→object parsing needed yet, so no YAML-parsing\n  dependency needed yet either — only `remark-frontmatter`, to isolate the block boundary). A\n  real key/value store is deliberately deferred, not abandoned.",
    "title": "00C6JRYTMG01A",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T18:36:24.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG01B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG01B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Broader direction (not this stage): `props` as one extensible mechanism, not one hardcoded\n  field per feature.** `ordered`/`start`/`checked` (`BlockNode`, shipped earlier this session)\n  are exactly the pattern this is meant to move away from — three separate, purpose-built typed\n  fields, one per feature, each requiring its own schema addition. The better long-term shape:\n  a single extensible `props` mechanism that both frontmatter *and* `ordered`/`start`/`checked`\n  eventually live inside, rather than every new piece of metadata minting its own field. Not\n  designed here — this doc only settles that frontmatter's *current* stage-appropriate answer is\n  the plain opaque field above; `ordered`/`start`/`checked` are **not** being touched or migrated\n  now (still their own fields, unchanged, working) — this is a direction flagged for a future\n  design pass once the shape of \"extensible props\" is actually worked out, not a change in\n  progress.",
    "title": "00C6JRYTMG01B",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T18:36:24.224Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG01C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG01C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Broader direction (not this stage): `props` as one extensible mechanism, not one hardcoded\n  field per feature.** `ordered`/`start`/`checked` (`BlockNode`, shipped earlier this session)\n  are exactly the pattern this is meant to move away from — three separate, purpose-built typed\n  fields, one per feature, each requiring its own schema addition. The better long-term shape:\n  a single extensible `props` mechanism that both frontmatter *and* `ordered`/`start`/`checked`\n  eventually live inside, rather than every new piece of metadata minting its own field. Not\n  designed here — this doc only settles that frontmatter's *current* stage-appropriate answer is\n  the plain opaque field above; `ordered`/`start`/`checked` are **not** being touched or migrated\n  now (still their own fields, unchanged, working) — this is a direction flagged for a future\n  design pass once the shape of \"extensible props\" is actually worked out, not a change in\n  progress.",
    "title": "00C6JRYTMG01C",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T18:36:24.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG01D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Not implemented: needs `remark-frontmatter` wired into the pipeline and `parseMarkdownTree`'s\nsignature (and callers — `artifacts.ts`'s `ingestArtifact`, `verifyPhase0.ts`) updated to\nextract and return the frontmatter body separately from the `BlockNode` tree.",
    "title": "00C6JRYTMG01D",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T18:36:24.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG01N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6JRYTMG01N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Investigated and confirmed, decision pending**: `remark-gfm` wiring + `table` handling (§4 —\nrecommend opaque-leaf treatment, same as `code`).",
    "title": "00C6JRYTMG01N",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T18:36:24.224Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6JRYTMG01P",
