  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6K5Y28000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6K5Y28000S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`table` — decided (opaque) and implemented.** `remark-gfm` now wired into `astParser.ts`'s\n  real pipeline (`.use(remarkParse).use(remarkGfm)`), which also genuinely fixes `checked` as a\n  coupled side effect (confirmed: `verifyPhase0.ts` now asserts on the actual `checked` value,\n  not just round-trip shape, and passes). `table` added to `isStructural` as one more opaque\n  leaf (`text = rawText`), same treatment as `code`/`thematicBreak`/`html` — no per-row/per-cell\n  decomposition; `table`'s own children come out empty for free, since `tableRow`/`tableCell`\n  aren't structural either, so nothing needs excluding explicitly. Added to `reconcile.ts`'s\n  `LEAF_TYPES` and `project.ts`'s leaf-passthrough case, same as the `thematicBreak`/`html` fix.\n  Verified: `verify:phase0 -- --db` clean, sample markdown extended with a real aligned table.\n  **Migration note, reasoned not yet forced**: three real artifacts (`Aperas-architecture.md`,\n  `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md`, `tdb-cli-status-walkthrough.md`) already contain real tables,\n  currently stored as opaque `paragraph`s from before this change — `kg:track`'s hash-gate means\n  they won't re-ingest until touched (same limitation noted in §4's `thematicBreak`/`html` entry\n  originally). When they do, the type change (`paragraph` → `table`) should reconcile cleanly\n  rather than showing as removed+added: `reconcile.ts`'s Stage A matches purely on `leafKey`'s\n  *string value* (`node.text`), never comparing `.type` between old and new — so a `paragraph`\n  and a `table` with byte-identical `text` (the same table, same raw slice, only the recognized\n  type differs) match as the same node, and `blockId` carries over. Reasoned from re-reading\n  `diffChildren`, not forced against real content this session.",
    "title": "00C6KAEKM800S",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T19:00:03.507Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6K5Y28000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6K5Y28000V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Wikilinks (`[[Page]]`, `[[Page|Alias]]`) — confirmed unrecognized, same non-loss-but-opaque\n  category as everything else inline.** Tested directly: plain `remark-parse` (with or without\n  `remark-gfm`) doesn't recognize wikilink syntax at all — no plugin for it is installed, and\n  nothing in CommonMark/GFM defines it. `[[Some Page]]` parses as one plain `text` node, brackets\n  included, verbatim — not even partially mis-parsed as an ordinary link. Contrast: an *ordinary*\n  `[text](url)` link **is** already recognized as a proper `link` mdast node by plain\n  `remark-parse` (core CommonMark, confirmed live) — but nothing extracts it either (the\n  pre-existing, already-tracked \"Fractal Ontology Enhancements\" gap). Wikilinks would need\n  their own plugin (e.g. `remark-wiki-link`) even to reach that same starting point. Per this\n  turn's decision on inline features generally: left as-is, not in scope for this doc.",
    "title": "00C6KAEKM800V",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T19:00:03.507Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
