    "children": [],
    "text": "item one",
    "title": "00C6Q3HNN8002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3HNN8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3HNN8003",
    "children": [],
    "text": "item two",
    "title": "00C6Q3HNN8003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3HQ30001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3HQ30001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3HQ30002",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3HQ30003"
    ],
    "text": "Intro sentence for the demo folder.",
    "title": "# Demo Folder",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false,
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3HQ30001/props/StringProp/JzuvXKj9EK9DLuPp",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3HQ30001/props/StringProp/Xm194MC3Pf-aOL6Z",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3HQ30002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3HQ30002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "item one",
    "title": "00C6Q3HQ30002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3HQ30003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3HQ30003",
    "children": [],
    "text": "item two",
    "title": "00C6Q3HQ30003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R000",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Prevention**: NTP uses gradual \"slew\" adjustments instead of \"step\" (instant jumps).",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R001",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Absorption**: The generator uses a high-water-mark (`max(now, last_emitted)`). Small backward jumps are absorbed by the sequence counter.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Failover**: If a backward jump is too large (risking counter overflow), the generator flips its anomaly bit to use a distinct failover machine ID, preventing collisions with its normal output.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R006",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`fileHash`**: Hash of the raw file's current content, recomputed on every `track` event.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R007",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`ingestedHash`**: Hash of the raw file's content as of the last confirmed sync (ingestion or projection).",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R00E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Inheritance**: Inherits from `BaseNode`. (This means links themselves possess a `links` array, allowing arbitrary depth for provenance or comments).",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R00E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R00F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Implicit Source**: Because a `BaseLink` resides within the `BaseNode.links` array, the node holding the array is implicitly the source.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R00J",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Inheritance**: Inherits from `BaseLink`.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R00J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R00K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Explicit Source**: Because it floats independently of any node's `links` array, it adds a `source` pointer to explicitly declare its origin.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R00K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R00Q",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00R"
    ],
    "text": "`BaseLink` is abstract too — the same gap as `BaseEdge`/`Assertion`, just noticed later, once `BlockNode.links` extraction (Aperas-markdown-fractal-mapping-design.md §4) actually needed to write one. `Link` is `BaseLink`'s one concrete leaf: no fields of its own, just makes the `target`/`predicate` (+ inherited `links`) lineage instantiable. Used for an inline Markdown link whose target resolves to an internal node (`[title]([[code]])`) — the `predicate` is always the fixed constant `\"references\"` for this use, distinguishing structural inline links from `Assertion`'s deliberately-chosen semantic predicates at query time.",
    "title": "### E. Link (The Concrete Intrinsic Edge)",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R00R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```json\n{\n  \"@id\": \"Link\",\n  \"@type\": \"Class\",\n  \"@inherits\": [\"BaseLink\"]\n}\n```",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R00R",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R00Y",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00Z"
    ],
    "text": "**Upward Breadcrumbs (Context Retrieval)**:\n   Because `BaseLink` is a fully addressable Document, it does not need a physical `parent` pointer. If a user addresses a leaf node directly (`BaseLink/123`), they can follow the breadcrumbs \"upward\" to find the parent context:",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R00Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R00Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```javascript\n   // What ParentNode has a 'links' property pointing to me?\n   WOQL.triple(\"v:ParentNode\", \"links\", \"BaseLink/123\")\n   ```",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R00Z",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R010",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R011",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R012"
    ],
    "text": "**Universal Backlink Tracing (Logseq/Roam style)**:\n   You can instantly query the entire graph for *anything* that points to a specific target node, regardless of the predicate or origin.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R010",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "```javascript\n   // What nodes point to this block, and via what relationship?\n   WOQL.triple(\"v:SourceNode\", \"v:Predicate\", \"BlockNode/MyTargetBlock\")\n   ```",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R011",
    "type": "code",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "This instantly returns every intrinsic `BaseLink`, extrinsic `BaseEdge`, or parent document that references the target, enabling ultra-fast, database-native backlink panels.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R012",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R015",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`README.md` Ingestion**: A separate `README.md` file is a legacy \"dumb folder\" workaround. The `README.md` is fully absorbed into the `FolderNode`. Its content populates the folder's `text` (abstract) and initial `children` blocks. The `README.md` is not exposed as a separate `ArtifactNode`.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R016",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`children`**: Contains other nested `FolderNode`s and `ArtifactNode`s, alongside the parsed block children from the `README.md`.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R016",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01D",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01E",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01F"
    ],
    "text": "**`title` (The Semantic Label)**: Used for wikilinks and graph queries.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false,
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01D/props/StringProp/9IHA463_VgF4Lid3",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01D/props/StringProp/Qzzp1ochUKur6mGX",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "For direct UI input: The author is prompted to provide a title.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "For Markdown ingestion: The parser uses an AI agent to summarize the block into a title. If AI is unavailable, it falls back to the block ID.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01G",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`text` (The Abstract/Body)**: The actual content shown in the current document.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01H",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`children`**: An ordered `List` of child `BlockNode`s.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01J",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01K",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01M"
    ],
    "text": "**`unfolded`**: A boolean flag representing the persistent view-state for UIs and Agents.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false,
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01J/props/StringProp/0D9yg9m0LEjImEOY",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01J/props/StringProp/WrijVTOasNTsg9e9",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01K",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Human UI & Agent Interface**: When rendering to a screen or an AI prompt, the graph defaults to *folded* (`false`) to manage cognitive/token overload. Only the current block's `text` and the children's `title`s are shown. If this flag is `true`, the subtree auto-expands on load.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Artifact Projection**: When syncing to a physical `.md` file, the tree is ALWAYS 100% unfolded (writing the full document to disk). This flag is ignored.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01R",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Artifact Projection (File Syncing)**: When the system serializes a graph back to a physical `.md` file, the tree is ALWAYS 100% unfolded. The persistent `unfolded` state is ignored, as the physical file must contain the entire document body. For `FolderNode`s, the block children are serialized back out to the folder's `README.md`.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Human UI (Phase 1 Web App)**: The UI is folded by default and traverses seamlessly across folder/file boundaries. Users see the `text` (abstract) of the current node (`FolderNode`, `ArtifactNode`, or `BlockNode`) and the abstracts of its direct children. Expanding a `FolderNode` reveals child files/folders and its own `README.md` blocks inline without context switching.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Agentic Interface (BFS Traversal)**: AI agents interact with the graph exactly like the Human UI to manage token limitations. They receive folded views and can navigate continuously from a workspace root `FolderNode` down to a deeply nested `BlockNode` using BFS tool calls to expand subtrees.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Intrinsic Links (`links`)**: Links and metadata (tags, properties) authored directly inside the node. Stored in `BaseNode.links`.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Extrinsic Edges (`BaseEdge`)**: Independent assertions created by external authors/agents. They float independently (to avoid mutating the source node) and are discovered via WOQL queries.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01X",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**UI Display**: The UI displays non-inline metadata/properties from `links` and queried extrinsic `BaseEdge`s in dedicated reference panels. Inline links remain rendered naturally inside the `text` body.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R01Z",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R020",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R021"
    ],
    "text": "**The Preview Mechanism**:",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R01Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false,
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01Z/props/StringProp/ASz2Rc1zP5q4V0yQ",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R01Z/props/StringProp/tbJStiXAyKs2faN3",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R020",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R020",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Human UI**: Humans receive the preview interactively by **hovering** over a link or wikilink in the UI, popping up the target block's abstract (`text`).",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R020",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R021",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R021",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Agent Interface**: Agents receive the target block's abstract (`text`) embedded directly in the `links` list returned by the projection/tool call, providing instant preview context without requiring UI hover triggers.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R021",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R022",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R022",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Manual Jump**: If the user or agent needs more context than the target's abstract, they manually \"jump\" to the target block to explore its children.",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R022",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3N69R023",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3N69R023",
    "children": [],
    "text": "---",
    "title": "00C6Q3N69R023",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000K",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000M",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000N",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q98B7G00K",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000Q",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000R",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000Y",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000Z"
    ],
    "text": "Links are **not** in the \"permanently out of scope\" bucket above — unlike bold/italic/etc.,\nextracting them was an already-designed feature\n(`Aperas-fractal-ontology-implementation-plan.md` Stage 2 item 4; tracked in\n`Aperas-dev-status.md`'s \"Fractal Ontology Enhancements\"): inline links become `Link` objects\n(the concrete `BaseLink` leaf — `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.E, added alongside this\nwork, the same gap `Assertion` already closed for `BaseEdge`) in `BlockNode.links`, `Link.target`\npointing at a real node.",
    "title": "### Implemented — `BlockNode.links` extraction",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000M",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Scope, clarified this turn**: extraction isn't wikilink-specific — it applies to *any* link\nwhose target resolves to an internal node reference (a snowflake code), not just wikilink syntax\nused on its own. The deciding factor is what the target *is* (internal code vs. external URL).\nA link to an external URL never becomes a `BaseLink`; there's nothing internal to target.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00H",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000N",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Corrected, confirmed live**: `[[...]]` isn't a separate, competing link syntax needing its own\nplugin — it's how the *target* of an ordinary link is written to signal \"this is an internal\ncode, not a URL\": `[internal link]([[00C5H15NT0000]])`. Tested directly: plain `remark-parse`\n(no plugin, no `remark-gfm`) already parses this as a completely ordinary `link` mdast node —\n`{ url: \"[[00C5H15NT0000]]\", children: [{ type: \"text\", value: \"internal link\" }] }` — exactly\nthe same node shape as `[external](https://example.com)` (confirmed side-by-side in the same\ntest), just with a different-looking `url` string. So the parsing half is *entirely* free\nalready, for both forms — no wikilink plugin needed at all for this project's actual usage. An\nearlier revision of this doc wrongly assumed `[[...]]` would be used the Obsidian/Logseq way (as\na standalone replacement for `[text](url)`, tested in isolation as bare `[[Some Page]]`) and\nconcluded a plugin like `remark-wiki-link` was required — that conclusion doesn't apply to the\nform actually being designed here.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000P",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Implemented, with one deliberate simplification.** Rather than walking mdast `link` nodes,\n`astParser.ts`'s `extractLinkCodes` regexes the already-captured raw `title`/`text` slice\ndirectly for `\\[[^\\]]*\\]\\(\\[\\[([^\\])]+)\\]\\]\\)` — every leaf's `title`/`text` is already a raw,\nbyte-for-byte source slice (§1), so this finds every occurrence uniformly across every block\ntype with no need to special-case which mdast node kind it's nested in. Since this pure,\nDB-less parser can't resolve a code into a real node id, it only captures the raw codes onto an\nephemeral `ParsedBlockNode.linkCodes` field (never written to the DB); `artifacts.ts`'s\n`resolveBlockLinks` (which has DB access) resolves each one at ingestion time and replaces it\nwith a real `links: [{\"@type\": \"Link\", target, predicate: \"references\"}]` entry, deleting\n`linkCodes` before the tree is written.",
    "title": "00C6Q3P89000P",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-08-30T23:23:16.767Z",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000Q",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Authoring convention, settled — bare `[[code]]` never needs parser support at all.** The\ncanonical stored form is always `[title]([[code]])` — a human never has to hand-type that. The\n(unbuilt) Human UI is where a bare `[[code]]` — typed or pasted — gets auto-expanded into the\nfull `[title]([[code]])` form, filling in `title` for the human, before it's ever saved as\nMarkdown. This closes the wikilink question definitively: there is no scenario where the\nMarkdown *parser* needs to understand standalone `[[...]]` on its own — that form only exists\ntransiently as a UI input convenience, never in a saved file. A wikilink plugin genuinely isn't\nneeded, not now and not later, unless a future decision changes what gets *saved*.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00M",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000R",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000S",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000T",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000V",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000W",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000X"
    ],
    "text": "**Open questions, found on audit — resolved:**",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00N",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false,
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000R/props/StringProp/5PVPZELPJssLccpa",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000R/props/StringProp/Rpg3L3E2QAeCSG53",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000S",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**What does the inner code resolve against, and what about dangling references?** Resolved via\n  the same addressing scheme used elsewhere (`resolveDirectOrSnowflake`, `directResolve.ts`): a\n  full node id, or a bare snowflake code (tried as `BlockNode`, then `ArtifactNode`, then\n  `FolderNode` — Snowflake ids share one generation scheme, so a bare code alone doesn't say\n  which). Resolution is best-effort and non-fatal: an unresolvable code (typo, forward reference,\n  or a target genuinely gone) is skipped with a console warning, never fails the whole\n  artifact's ingestion — confirmed live with a deliberately-dangling `[[ZZZZZZZZZZZZZ]]` code.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000T",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**`Link.predicate` value?** A fixed constant, `\"references\"` — not the link's visible text\n  (arbitrary, not a stable relation name); distinguishes structural inline links from\n  `Assertion`'s deliberately-chosen semantic predicates at query time.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000V",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Does extraction touch `text`?** No — confirmed as implemented: `text`/`title` stay the exact\n  raw slice, `links` is a purely additive index built from a *copy* of the matched substrings,\n  never a mutation of the leaf's own content.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000W",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Multiple links / `Set` ordering?** Left as `Set<Link>`, no ordering added — `links` remains a\n  lookup index only, `text` is always the rendering/reading-order source of truth.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000X",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Reconciliation/projection consequences?** None needed, confirmed (not just inferred) by the\n  live round-trip tests in `verifyPhase0.ts`: `text` is unaffected, so reconciliation and\n  projection both continue to work unchanged.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000Y",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**One real prerequisite gap found during implementation, not previously flagged even in this\naudit**: `BaseLink` is `@abstract`, and — unlike `BaseEdge`, which already had `Assertion` as its\none concrete leaf — nothing inherited directly from `BaseLink` was instantiable at all.\n`BlockNode.links: Set<BaseLink>` literally couldn't be written to until a concrete `Link` class\nwas added (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.E), mirroring `Assertion` exactly (no fields of\nits own, just makes the lineage instantiable).",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00V",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89000Z",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**A genuine reference cycle, discovered live while extending `verifyPhase0.ts`'s cleanup for\nthis feature**: a block whose `links` field points at a `Link`, which in turn `target`s some\nother block (a self-link makes this a literal cycle back to the same root) can't be cleaned up\nby deleting the `Link` and the blocks as separate sequential calls — each side fails as\nstill-referenced by the other. TerminusDB's referential-integrity-on-delete check only allows a\nreference from *outside* the set of documents being deleted in one call, so the fix is deleting\nthe `Link` ids together with the blocks that form the cycle, in one combined batch\n(`findLinkIdsTargeting`, `crud.ts`) — not a design change, but a real operational detail anyone\nwriting cleanup/deletion code touching `Link` needs to know.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G00W",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89001A",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001B",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001C",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001D",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001E",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001F"
    ],
    "text": "**Open questions, resolved:**",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G017",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false,
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001A/props/StringProp/2KNdfKOaYLJMTw2X",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001A/props/StringProp/Id5IetXT08Bv71Cq",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89001B",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`FolderNode` isn't a `BlockNode`, so it has no mdast `type` for `serializeBlock`'s dispatch to\n    key on — but no wrapper was needed at all: `renderChildren` never switches on `node.type`\n    itself (only `serializeBlock`'s dispatch does), so `serializeFolderToReadme` just calls it\n    directly against the `FolderNode`, emitting `folder.text` (the consumed leading sentence)\n    ahead of it.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G018",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89001C",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Frontmatter round-trip: yes, for both kinds. A shared `withFrontmatter` helper in `project.ts`\n    reads `getProp(node, 'frontmatter')` and prepends a re-emitted `---\\n...\\n---\\n\\n` block —\n    fixing the same pre-existing gap in `ArtifactNode` projection at the same time (it never\n    re-emitted frontmatter either, until now).",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G019",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89001D",
    "children": [],
    "text": "Read path: a small purpose-built `getFolderTreeViaGraphQL`, not a fully generic \"any node\"\n    abstraction. It uses the hybrid polymorphism pattern from §7's GraphQL findings: `_type`/\n    `_json` for the one polymorphic `FolderNode.children` hop, then reuses the *existing*\n    `fetchBlockSubtree`/truncation-refetch machinery (now exported from `graphql.ts`) for each\n    `BlockNode` child's own concrete subtree — no duplicated logic, and no need for the plain\n    Document API fallback originally guessed at here.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G01A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89001E",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Corrected from the original proposal**: `kg:project` writes to disk **by default** for\n    both `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` (a `--dry-run` flag prints instead) — not print-only as\n    first proposed. `Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §1.B is explicit that once a tree is\n    ingested, *\"the DB becomes the source of truth. Edits are made directly in the DB, and\n    artifact files are regenerated (projected) from it\"* — re-ingestion is named the *fallback*\n    path, only for hand-edits outside the DB. The original print-only proposal had this backwards\n    (an artifact of Phase 0 not yet having DB-native content-authoring tools, which made\n    file-editing the *practical* norm so far — not the intended end-state).",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G01B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P89001F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P89001F",
    "children": [],
    "text": "`FolderNode.children` mixes the README's own `BlockNode`s with references to nested\n    `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode` documents — `serializeFolderToReadme` filters `children` down to\n    `BlockNode`-typed entries (identified by the absence of a GraphQL `_type` tag, which\n    `getFolderTreeViaGraphQL` only attaches to the reference stubs it doesn't inline) before\n    calling `renderChildren`, exactly as proposed.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7G01C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P898011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P898011",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Implemented and verified — `BlockNode.links` extraction** (§4's last subsection): a new\nconcrete `Link` class (`Aperas-core-ontology-design.md` §2.E — `BaseLink` was abstract with no\nconcrete leaf at all, a real prerequisite gap found while implementing this), `astParser.ts`'s\npure `extractLinkCodes` capturing raw `[[code]]` targets, `artifacts.ts`'s `resolveBlockLinks`\nresolving them at ingestion time (best-effort, `directResolve.ts`'s shared full-id/bare-snowflake\nresolution). `verify:phase0 -- --db` exercises both a resolving and a deliberately-dangling link.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7R001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P898012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P898012",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Implemented and verified — `FolderNode` → `README.md` projection** (§6's second finding):\n`graphql.ts`'s `getFolderTreeViaGraphQL`, `project.ts`'s `serializeFolderToReadme`/\n`projectFolderToReadme`, `kgCli.ts`'s `kg:project` extended to accept a folder path and to\n**write to disk by default** (corrected from an earlier print-only proposal — see §6's resolved\nopen questions). `verify:phase0 -- --db` confirms the full project → write → re-ingest → project\ncycle is a stable fixed point.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7R002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q3P898013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q3P898013",
    "children": [],
    "text": "**Deferred deliberately**: inline features (§4, bold/italic/strikethrough/footnotes) confirmed\npermanently out of scope — no future revisit implied.",
    "title": "00C6Q98B7R003",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q8CPWR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q8CPWR000",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q8CPWR001"
    ],
    "title": "Document Root",
    "type": "root",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q8CPWR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q8CPWR001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q8CPWR002"
    ],
    "text": "A real link: [the roadmap]([[00C5FP8F2G000]]).",
    "title": "# Probe Codespan",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false,
    "links": [
      "Link/konApuephPfot3C6"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q8CPWR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q8CPWR002",
    "children": [],
    "text": "An inert example in code: `[title]([[code]])` should not extract.",
    "title": "00C6Q8CPWR002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "unfolded": false
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q8SJ6R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q8SJ6R001",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode/00C6Q8SJ6R002",
      "BlockNode/00C6Q8SJ6R003"
    ],
    "text": "Intro sentence for the demo folder.",
    "title": "# Demo Folder",
    "type": "heading",
    "unfolded": false,
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q8SJ6R001/props/StringProp/JxOWLmHwW9NJ3N0o",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q8SJ6R001/props/StringProp/kAr7CRHxC7w4g5oD",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode/00C6Q8SJ6R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "blockId": "00C6Q8SJ6R002",
    "children": [],
